  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "about": "Woodcore's look, written once (v0.90): the website's CSS custom properties, which website/build.py writes into assets/site.css, and the window's palette and style sheet, which calc/tools/theme.py builds from the same values. A name is a CSS custom property without its two dashes. The site-only tokens (shadow, code-bg, syn-*) and the window-only ones (on-primary, override, warning, danger, ok, lit, desk, card) sit beside the shared ones rather than in files of their own, so that every colour of Woodcore is in this one file. The canvas tokens (plan-*, drawing-*, annex-*, badge-ink; v0.117, issue #29) name what a colour does on the window's drawing surfaces -- a selection, a snap, a track, a grid -- rather than its hue, and have the same value in both schemes: they are drawn on the sheet, which stays paper-white in either (docs/ui/window.md §10quater). Read once when their module is imported, which is right only while the two values are equal -- tests/test_theme.py holds them so.",
